w: Sa- vior, a- gain to Thy dear name we raise With one ac- cord our part- ing hymn of praise;
w: Grant us Thy peace up- on our home- ward way; With Thee be- gan, with Thee shall end the day.
w: Grant us Thy peace, through this ap- proach- ing night; Turn Thou for us its dark- ness in- to light;
w: Grant us Thy peace through- out our earth- ly life; Peace to Thy church from er- ror and from strife;
w: Thy peace in life, the balm of ev- ery pain; Thy peace in death, the hope to rise a- gain;
w: Fa- ther, once more be- fore we part, we raise With one ac- cord our part- ing hymn of praise:
d2 G G | c2 c2 | c A B c | B4 | G2 A G | G2 E2 | D D E D | D4 |]
w: We stand to bless Thee ere our wor- ship cease; Then, low- ly kneel- ing, wait Thy word of peace.
w: Guard thou the lips from sin, the hearts from shame, That in this house have called up- on Thy name.
w: From harm and dan- ger keep Thy child- ren free, For dark and light are both a- like to Thee.
w: Peace to our land, the fruit of truth and love; Peace in each heart, Thy Spi- rit from a- bove.
w: Then, when Thy voice shall bid our con- flict cease, Call us, O Lord, to Thine e- ter- nal peace.
w: Once more we bless Thee, ere our songs shall cease, Then, low- ly knee- ling, pray Thee for Thy peace.
